; STORE-SHELL §4/§5: corruption propagates along the typing edge.
;
; The corrupted object is a SCHEMA that a stored entity depends on. Two violations, of
; two different classes: WF1 on the schema itself, and the entity's typing precondition
; (STORE-MODEL §5, boundary check 4) — its schema address is still PRESENT, so WF2 is
; satisfied, but it no longer RESOLVES, because `getChecked` refuses bytes that do not
; hash to their address.

(schema-put (object (f "alpha" req (prim int))))
(entity-put @1 (obj ("alpha" (i 1))))
(check)
(assert-code prev 0)

(corrupt @1 3 80)
(check)
(assert-code prev 1)
